# Input file for multiscatter
#
# This example is of cirrus cloud and aerosol sampled by a the
# spaceborne Calipso lidar
#
# The first line contains 
#  1: Number of range gates in profile
#  2: Lidar wavelength (m)
#  3: Altitude of lidar (m)
#  4: Laser divergence, 1/e half-width (radians)
#  5: Telescope field-of-view, half-width (radians)
# The subsequent lines contain
#  1: Range of gate above ground starting with nearest gate to lidar (m)
#  2: Extinction coefficient of cloud/aerosol only (m-1)
#  3: Equivalent squared-area cloud/aerosol radius (m)
#  4: Extinction-to-backscatter ratio of cloud/aerosol (sr)
#  5: Air extinction coefficient (m-1)
# 
# To run the code do this:
#  ./multiscatter < calipso_cirrus_aerosol_example.in
# For better results you might wish to try the following options:
#  ./multiscatter -wide-angle-cutoff 0.1
#
